# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows dev machine, and a line-ending rewrite inside a
# TTF is a corrupt font — a failure that surfaces only when a PDF renders. Git's own
# binary detection would very likely catch these anyway; this makes it certain.
*.ttf binary

# The request-contract snapshot is compared against a string the test BUILDS with LF endings
# (review B-36). core.autocrlf would hand a fresh Windows checkout CRLF, so the comparison could
# never be equal — the suite was green only on the machine whose own run had rewritten the file.
# Pinned to LF here, and both sides are normalised in the test too, because a working copy that
# predates this line is still out there. The PWA carries the same pair of rules for its own copy.
src/test/resources/contract/*.json text eol=lf
